Tracey
======

Tracey is a compiler for the Tracey programming language (`.trc` files).
It is written in ISO C17 and targets AArch64 Linux. The compiler can
produce assembly, or assemble and link it into a native executable in one
step.

Status
------

Tracey is in the bootstrap stage. The compiler is under active development
and is not yet considered stable. Language syntax, compiler internals, and
project structure may change before the first public release. Breaking
changes may occur without notice.

What works today
----------------

- Functions with parameters, including `void`, and forward references.
- Local variables: `int`, `bool`, `char`, `short`, `long`, `float`,
  `double`, `unsigned`/`signed` variants, `size_t`, and pointers.
- Fixed-size arrays that decay to pointers.
- Statements: `if`/`else`, `while`, `for`, `break`, `continue`, `goto`,
  labels, `return`, blocks, and expression statements.
- Expressions: arithmetic, comparisons, logical, bitwise, ternary `?:`,
  assignment and compound assignment, indexing, address-of, and dereference.
- A small standard library: `print`, `printf`, `input_int`, `input_str`.
- A C-like preprocessor: `#include`, `#define`, `#ifdef`, `#ifndef`,
  `#if`, `#endif`, `#defined`.
- An internal AArch64 assembler and linker that produce ELF64 executables.

Repository layout
-----------------

- `general/` — compiler source code
- `include/` — public headers
- `dependencies/` — external dependencies (none required at build time)
- `docs/` — documentation
- `etc/` — project configuration presets
- `lib/` — standard library headers and implementations
- `runtime/` — mini runtime notes
- `test/` — C unit tests
- `tests/` — end-to-end language tests
- `tools/` — compiler, assembler, and linker drivers
- `build/` — build output (generated)

See `docs/README` for the documentation index.

Development
-----------

Tracey is developed in ISO C17. The build uses GNU Make and Python 3
(for Kconfig).

Build
-----

```bash
make          # build traceyc, traceyas, traceyld, and the tests
make test     # run unit tests and end-to-end language tests
make clean    # remove the build directory
```

See `docs/build.md` for full build instructions, including configuration
presets and sanitizers.

Coding style
------------

All C code follows `AGENTS.md`. See `docs/maintenance.md`.

Contributing
------------

Contributions, bug reports, and suggestions are welcome. As the language
is still in early development, breaking changes may occur without notice.

Note
----

The project moved its primary hosting to GitHub. Repository activity is
supported on both platforms for contributors who prefer either one.
